    {
      "id": "brake-caliper",
      "name": {
        "en": "Rim brake",
        "zh": "轮圈刹车"
      },
      "group": "brake",
      "summary": {
        "en": "Squeezes rubber pads against the rim.",
        "zh": "把橡胶刹车块夹紧在轮圈上。"
      },
      "detail": {
        "en": "Two arms with a rubber pad on each, one on each side of the metal rim [S1]. Squeezed, the pads rub on the rim and friction slows the wheel: in this model a light squeeze stops it in about 1.8 s and a firm squeeze in about 0.6 s [S1, S29].\n\nWet rims make rim brakes work less well, so cyclists start braking earlier in the rain [S18, S19].",
        "zh": "两只夹臂，各装一块橡胶刹车块，分别在金属轮圈的两侧 [S1]。一捏刹车，刹车块就擦着轮圈，摩擦力让轮子慢下来：在这个模型里，轻捏约 1.8 s 停下，用力捏约 0.6 s 停下 [S1, S29]。\n\n轮圈湿了，轮圈刹车的效果会变差，所以下雨天骑车要早一点刹车 [S18, S19]。"
      },
